{
  "manufacturer": "Huawei",
  "manufacturer_slug": "huawei",
  "model": "SmartLogger plant data logger (Modbus TCP)",
  "model_slug": "smartlogger",
  "short_model": "SmartLogger",
  "aliases": [
    "Huawei SmartLogger"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Solar inverter gateway (plant data logger)",
  "applies_to": "Huawei SmartLogger (V100R001C00 to V300R001C00 firmware families) per ModBus Interface Definitions issue 35; the document names only 'SmartLogger', so check the issue that matches your hardware and firmware.",
  "summary": "The SmartLogger is Huawei's plant data logger. Over Modbus TCP it answers for itself with logical device ID 0 and reaches inverters, power meters and environment monitors behind it by their RS485 addresses. This map covers the SmartLogger's own registers: clock, power on/off and transfer trip, active and reactive power adjustment, plant totals for power, current, voltage and energy, plant status, scheduling modes and targets, capacity values, DI status and alarm bit words.",
  "transport": [
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 0,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are sent as printed: the read example requests register 32306 with address bytes 7E 32. In Modbus TCP the SmartLogger's own registers use logical device ID 0."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "SmartLogger V100R001C00 / V100R002C00 / V200R001C00 / V300R001C00 or later",
  "source": {
    "title": "SmartLogger ModBus Interface Definitions",
    "doc_number": "Issue 35",
    "revision_date": "2020-02-20",
    "url": "https://community.symcon.de/uploads/short-url/rIF4NzZBqBfB7S5WtTWW5jRamGn.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 2 (firmware), pp. 3-12 (SmartLogger registers), pp. 12-16 (alarm bits), pp. 25-27 (encoding, examples)",
    "unofficial": true
  },
  "notes": [
    "Huawei hosts this document only behind a support-site login; the copy linked is a forum upload of the unaltered Huawei PDF.",
    "Data encoding is big-endian for addresses and data (leftmost byte first), so 32- and 64-bit values are read high word first (ABCD).",
    "Gain is a divisor: a value with gain 10 in kW is read as raw / 10 kW.",
    "RO registers accept only function 03; WO registers accept only 06/16; RW accept all three.",
    "Left out: City (40002, no coding given), Reserved (40608), Device operation (40725, mixed ESN + command block), the reactive scheduling target (40742) whose gain is 10 or 1000 depending on mode, Japanese-utility communication registers 41942-41949 (gain marked N/A), current error during scanning (42150), and the power meter, weather station and remapped register sections.",
    "Alarm info 3 (50002, certificate alarms) appears only in the alarm table, so it is not listed.",
    "The document gives Modbus TCP port 502."
  ],
